'''Ann H. Gillespie''' {{born|8|August|1957}} is an actress who played two ''[[Star Trek]]'' roles, with her largest being the [[DS9 recurring characters|recurring character]] of [[Nurse]] [[Jabara]], whom she played four times in the first three seasons of {{s|DS9}}. Gillespie had earlier portrayed [[Ensign]] [[Hildebrant]] in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 2|second season]] episode {{e|Pen Pals}}. In 1984, Gillespie married the future fellow ''Next Generation'' and {{s|VOY}} guest actor [[Jeff Allin]]. {{el|post-gazette.com/ae/tv-radio/2008/09/10/TV-Notes-Actress-balances-90210-role-priesthood/stories/200809100204}} 

She is probably best known for her recurring role as Jackie Taylor in {{wt|Beverly Hills, 90210}}, whom Gillespie played throughout the series' ten year run. Her career on ''90210'' had her working alongside [[Michael Durrell]], [[Stanley Kamel]], [[Kerrie Keane]], [[Dina Meyer]] and [[Noley Thornton]]. From 2008 to 2009, Gillespie reprised her role as Jackie Taylor in six episodes of its successor ''90210''.

Gillespie also guest starred in {{wt|Happy Days}}, {{wt|Matlock (1986 TV series)|Matlock}} (with [[Corbin Bernsen]] and [[Granville Van Dusen]]), {{wt|Hunter (1984 American TV series)|Hunter}} (1990, starring [[Charles Hallahan]], with [[Leslie Bevis]]) and {{wt|7th Heaven (TV series)|7th Heaven}} (starring [[Stephen Collins]] and [[Catherine Hicks]]).

Gillespie received a BA degree from Goddard College in 2003. She is also an Episcopal priest, and uses the names '''Mother Ann Gillespie''' and '''Rev. Ann Gillespie'''.

