'''Leland Orser''' {{born|6|August|1960}} is an actor who appeared as [[Gai]] in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 2|second season]] episode {{e|Sanctuary}}, {{dis|Lovok|Changeling}} in the [[DS9 Season 3|third season]] episode {{e|The Die is Cast}}, [[Dejaren]] in the {{s|VOY}} [[VOY Season 4|fourth season]] episode {{e|Revulsion}}, and {{dis|Loomis|21st century}} in the {{s|ENT}} [[ENT Season 3|third season]] episode {{e|Carpenter Street}}.

For the VOY episode "Revulsion", he filmed his scenes between Monday {{d|14|July|1997}} and Thursday {{d|17|July|1997}} and on second unit on Thursday {{d|21|August|1997}} on [[Paramount Stage 16]]. His costume from this episode was later sold off on the [[It's A Wrap! sale and auction]] on eBay. {{stala|1135}} His costume from the episode "The Die is Cast" was also sold off. {{stala|3482}}

Orser has also appeared in several other films such as {{wt|Seven (1995 film)|Seven}} (1995), {{wt|Independence Day (1996 film)|Independence Day}} (1996, with [[Brent Spiner]] and [[Erick Avari]]) {{wt|Saving Private Ryan}} (1998), {{wt|Pearl Harbor (film)|Pearl Harbor}} (2001, with [[Randy Oglesby]] and [[Raphael Sbarge]]), {{wt|Daredevil (film)|Daredevil}} (2003, with [[Erick Avari]] and [[Jude Ciccolella]]), {{wt|Confidence (2003 film)|Confidence}} (2003, with [[Tommy "Tiny" Lister, Jr.]]) and {{wt|Alien Resurrection}} (1997, starring [[Winona Ryder]], with [[Raymond Cruz]], [[Ron Perlman]] and [[Brad Dourif]]). He also had a recurring role on {{wt|ER (TV series)|ER}} as Dr. Lucien Dubenko. He later appeared in all three of {{wt|Taken (franchise)|Taken}} film series as Sam Gilroy (2008-2014). He guest starred in a season 7 episode of {{wt|The Golden Girls}} (with [[Nicholas Kepros]], [[Zach Grenier]], and [[Tony Plana]]).

From 2016 to 2019, he was a regular on {{wt|Berlin Station (TV series)|Berlin Station}}, along with [[Michelle Forbes]], [[Tamlyn Tomita]], [[Ashley Judd]], and [[James Cromwell]], and went on to have a lead role on {{wt|American Gigolo (TV series)|American Gigolo}} (2022).

