'''Kevin Conway''' {{born|29|May|1942|died|5|February|2020}} was the actor who played {{dis|Kahless|clone}} in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 6|sixth season]] episode {{e|Rightful Heir}}.

In 1980, he starred as Dr. William Haber alongside [[Bruce Davison]] in {{wt|The Lathe of Heaven (film)|The Lathe of Heaven}}. On stage, Conway co-starred [[Philip Anglim]] in the Broadway play ''The Elephant Man''. Later, in 1982, the two reprised their roles in a made-for-television adaptation of the play. In 1988, he appeared in {{wt|Funny Farm (film)|Funny Farm}} (1988, with [[Mike Starr]], [[William Newman]], [[Dan Desmond]], [[Reg E. Cathey]], [[David Williams]], and [[Dakin Matthews]]).

Conway co-starred in {{wt|Gettysburg (1993 film)|Gettysburg}} (1993) and {{wt|Gods and Generals}} (2003). [[W. Morgan Sheppard]], [[Billy Campbell]] and [[Joseph Fuqua]] starred in both of these films. Conway had turned down the role of Théoden in the ''Lord of the Rings'' films to recreate his ''Gettysburg'' role of Buster Kilrain in ''Gods and Generals.''

Conway appeared as himself and the Earl of Hastings in {{wt|Looking for Richard}} (1996), which also starred [[Richard Cox]], [[Winona Ryder]], [[Paul Guilfoyle]], [[Harris Yulin]], and [[F. Murray Abraham]], taking parts in a mock production of [[William Shakespeare]]'s ''[[Richard III]]''.

Conway appeared in {{wt|Mercury Rising}} (1998, written by [[Lawrence Konner]] and [[Mark Rosenthal]]). He also played General {{w|Curtis LeMay}} in {{wt|Thirteen Days (film)|Thirteen Days}} (2000), with [[Jack Blessing]], [[Len Cariou]], [[Charles Esten]], [[Tim Kelleher]], [[Boris Krutonog]], [[Ed Lauter]], and [[Bill Smitrovich]], [[Jack Blessing]], [[Bruce Greenwood]] (as [[John F. Kennedy]]) and [[Steven Culp]]), and appeared in {{wt|Black Knight (film)|Black Knight}} (2001, with [[Kevin P. Stillwell]]).

Conway had a recurring role as Seamus O'Reilly on {{wt|Oz (TV series)|Oz}}. He also provided the "Control Voice" for the 1995-2002 revival of ''The Outer Limits'', a role he took over from [[Vic Perrin]]. Several ''Star Trek'' alumni appeared in guest roles throughout the series, including [[Erich Anderson]], [[René Auberjonois]], [[Daniel Benzali]], [[Corbin Bernsen]], [[Clancy Brown]], [[Len Cariou]], [[Kim Cattrall]], [[Bill Cobbs]], [[Ronny Cox]], [[Roger Cross]], [[Brett Cullen]], [[Bruce Davison]], [[Nicole de Boer]], [[John de Lancie]], [[Michael Dorn]], [[Larry Drake]], [[Kirsten Dunst]], [[Michelle Forbes]], [[Robert Foxworth]], [[Bruce French]], [[Matt Frewer]], [[Megan Gallagher]], [[Joel Grey]], [[Bob Gunton]], [[Clint Howard]], [[Robert Ito]], [[Doug Jones]], [[Daniel Hugh Kelly]], [[Wallace Langham]], [[Andrea Martin]], [[Malcolm McDowell]], [[Stephen McHattie]], [[Robert Duncan McNeill]], [[Dina Meyer]], [[Leonard Nimoy]], [[France Nuyen]], [[Leland Orser]], [[Ron Perlman]], [[Robert Picardo]], [[Amanda Plummer]], [[Paul Popowich]], [[Harve Presnell]], [[Claire Rankin]], [[Saul Rubinek]], [[Alan Ruck]], [[William Sadler]], [[Chris Sarandon]], [[Michael Sarrazin]], [[John Savage]], [[Alan Scarfe]], [[Dwight Schultz]], [[Marina Sirtis]], [[Brent Spiner]], [[David Ogden Stiers]], [[Kate Vernon]], [[Nana Visitor]], [[David Warner]], [[Wil Wheaton]] and [[Dey Young]].

