'''Sandra Nelson''' {{born|29|December|1964}} is the actress who played [[Marayna]] in the {{s|VOY}} [[VOY Season 3|third season]] episode {{e|Alter Ego}} and [[Tavana]] in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 5|fifth season]] episode {{e|Soldiers of the Empire}}. Her dress from "Alter Ego" was later re-used by background actress [[Fedra Thompson]] in the episode {{e|Concerning Flight}} and sold off on the [[It's A Wrap! sale and auction]] on eBay. {{stala|9312}}

She was a regular cast member on {{wt|The Young and the Restless}} from 1997 through 1999. However, the majority of her credits from the 1990s are composed of made-for-television movies. These include {{wt|A Child Too Many}} (1993, with [[Stephen Macht]]), 1994's ''Voices from Within'' with [[Corbin Bernsen]], 1996's ''Brothers of the Frontier'' (with {{s|TNG}} star [[Jonathan Frakes]]), and 1996's ''Run for the Dream: The Gail Devers Story'' (with [[John Schuck]]).

In recent years, however, Nelson has branched out into motion pictures. She had roles in {{wt|Life as a House}} (2001, featuring {{s|ENT}} star [[Scott Bakula]] and ''Deep Space Nine'' guest actor [[Art Chudabala]]), and {{wt|De-Lovely}} (2004). Both films were directed by her father-in-law, Irwin Winkler. She also appeared in {{wt|Enough (film)|Enough}} (2002, with [[Billy Campbell]], [[Bill Cobbs]], [[Bruce French]], and [[Jeff Kober]]) and {{wt|The Wolf of Wall Street (2013 film)|The Wolf of Wall Street}} (2013).

