'''Michael Durrell''' {{born|6|October|1943}} is the actor from Brooklyn, New York, who played [[Hazar]] in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 2|second season]] episode {{e|Sanctuary}}.

Durrell is best known for his role as Robert Maxwell in the 1983 NBC mini series ''V''; he reprised his role as Maxwell in the 1984 sequel ''V: The Final Battle''. He also appeared in the first episode of ''V: The Series'' as Maxwell. (''V'' and ''V: The Final Battle'' also featured [[Andrew Prine]] and [[Richard Herd]]. ''V: The Final Battle'' also featured [[Dick Miller]] and [[Mark L. Taylor]]) 

Durrell was a main cast member in {{wt|Matlock (1986 TV series)|Matlock}} from 1986 to 1990. He reprised the role in the 1991 television movie ''Matlock: The Suspect.'' He also had a recurring role as Dr. John Martin in {{wt|Beverly Hills, 90210}} from 1993 to 2000 (with [[Ann Gillespie]]). Durrell also guest starred in {{wt|The Mindy Project}}, {{wt|Desperate Housewives}}, {{wt|ER (TV series)|ER}}, {{wt|Knight Rider (1982 TV series)|Knight Rider}} (1983, starring [[William Daniels]] and [[Patricia McPherson]]), {{wt|Remington Steele}} (starring [[Pierce Brosnan]]), {{wt|Mrs. Columbo}} (starring [[Kate Mulgrew]]), {{wt|Silk Stalkings}}, {{wt|NYPD Blue}} (2004, starring [[Gordon Clapp]], with [[Salli Elise Richardson]], [[Jude Ciccolella]], [[Scott Burkholder]] and [[Victor Raider Wexler]]), and {{wt|Dexter (TV series)|Dexter}} (2010, with [[Peter Weller]] and [[Scott Grimes]]).

In 1992, he appeared in {{wt|Sister Act}} starring [[Whoopi Goldberg]], with [[Jenifer Lewis]] and [[Max Grodénchik]]. In 2005, he starred in two motion pictures and a television movie. In ''Rumor Has It'' he starred with [[Andy Milder]], [[Jordan Lund]] and [[Christopher McDonald]]. In {{wt|Magma: Volcanic Disaster}} (2006) he played the [[President of the United States]]. He later appeared in ''Bald'' (2008). Durrell's first motion picture debut came in {{wt|Thank God It's Friday (film)|Thank God It's Friday}} (1980, with stunts coordinated by {{s|TOS}} stuntman [[Phil Adams]]). He starred in {{wt|The American Success Company}} (1980, with fellow ''Deep Space Nine'' guest [[John Glover]]), and also appeared in {{wt|Bayou Romance}} (1982, starring [[Michael Ansara]]) and {{wt|Defending Your Life}} (1991, with [[Julie Cobb]], [[Ken Thorley]] and [[Time Winters]]).

