'''Norman Snow''' {{born|29|March|1950|d|28|November|2022}} was the actor who played [[Torin]] in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 6|sixth season]] episode {{e|Rightful Heir}}.

[[Star Trek birthdays#March|Hailing]] from Little Rock, Arkansas, Snow is best known for playing the evil Xur in {{wt|The Last Starfighter}} (1984, with [[Marc Alaimo]], [[Barbara Bosson]], [[Kay E. Kuter]], [[Meg Wyllie]], and [[Wil Wheaton]]). Snow appeared in a handful of other films, including {{wt|The Europeans (1979 film)|The Europeans}} (1979) and {{wt|Manhunter (film)|Manhunter}} (1986).

Snow was a veteran of television daytime soap operas, having had recurring roles on {{wt|The Edge of Night}}, {{wt|As the World Turns}}, ''Guiding Light'', {{wt|General Hospital}}, ''Another World'', and {{wt|Days of Our Lives}}. He also made guest appearances on {{wt|Spenser: For Hire}}, starring [[Avery Brooks]], in 1986; and {{wt|Quantum Leap (1989 TV series)|Quantum Leap}} in 1992, starring [[Scott Bakula]] and {{s|ENT}} guest actor [[Dean Stockwell]].

Other television series on which Snow appeared include {{wt|Crime Story (American TV series)|Crime Story}} (1987, starring [[Bill Smitrovich]] and [[Billy Campbell]], with [[David Soul]]), {{wt|L.A. Law}} (1993, starring [[Corbin Bernsen]], with [[Robert Curtis Brown]], [[Samantha Eggar]], [[Harvey Jason]], [[Lawrence Tierney]] and [[Tom Wright]]), {{wt|Law & Order}}, {{wt|Beverly Hills, 90210}}, and two episodes of {{wt|Profiler (TV series)|Profiler}} (one with [[Craig Wasson]] and another with [[Lawrence Dobkin]]). Additionally, he was seen in such television movies as ''Going Underground'' (with [[Bruce McGill]]), ''Two Voices'' (with [[Vaughn Armstrong]] and [[Casey Biggs]]), and ''Hefner: Unauthorized'' (with [[Bill Bolender]], [[Pat Healy]] and [[Jim Metzler]]).

Snow passed away on November 28, 2022. {{el|arkansasonline.com/obituaries/2022/dec/11/norman-snow-jr-2022-12-11}}

